  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We answer yes to Problem 5.2 of Aivazidis, Loukaki and Müller (arXiv:2209.00986v2, p. 37; journal version, p. 1280): for every finite group G, H ≤ G and N normal in G, P_G(H) ≤ P_G(HN). Equality holds exactly when N ≤ H or H is normal in G. The same criterion with N = ker f characterizes equality in the homomorphism inequality (5.1). The note also proves the coprime-order assertion in Problem 5.3 and supplies a finite-quotient probability model for the finite-index setting in Problem 5.4.",
